#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:1
msgid "Import From Derivation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:3
msgid ""
"The value of a Nix expression can depend on the contents of a [store object]"
"(../store/store-object.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:7
msgid ""
"Passing an expression `expr` that evaluates to a [store path](../store/store-"
"path.md) to any built-in function which reads from the filesystem "
"constitutes Import From Derivation (IFD):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:9
msgid "[`import`](./builtins.md#builtins-import)` expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:10
msgid "[`builtins.readFile`](./builtins.md#builtins-readFile)` expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:11
msgid "[`builtins.readFileType`](./builtins.md#builtins-readFileType)` expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:12
msgid "[`builtins.readDir`](./builtins.md#builtins-readDir)` expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:13
msgid "[`builtins.pathExists`](./builtins.md#builtins-pathExists)` expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:14
msgid "[`builtins.filterSource`](./builtins.md#builtins-filterSource)` f expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:15
msgid "[`builtins.path`](./builtins.md#builtins-path)` { path = expr; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:16
msgid "[`builtins.hashFile`](./builtins.md#builtins-hashFile)` t expr`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:17
msgid "`builtins.scopedImport x drv`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:19
msgid ""
"When the store path needs to be accessed, evaluation will be paused, the "
"corresponding store object [realised](../glossary.md#gloss-realise), and "
"then evaluation resumed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:23
msgid ""
"This has performance implications: Evaluation can only finish when all "
"required store objects are realised. Since the Nix language evaluator is "
"sequential, it only finds store paths to read from one at a time. While "
"realisation is always parallel, in this case it cannot be done for all "
"required store paths at once, and is therefore much slower than otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:28
msgid ""
"Realising store objects during evaluation can be disabled by setting [`allow-"
"import-from-derivation`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-allow-import-from-"
"derivation) to `false`. Without IFD it is ensured that evaluation is "
"complete and Nix can produce a build plan before starting any realisation."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:31
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:33
msgid ""
"In the following Nix expression, the inner derivation `drv` produces a file "
"with contents `hello`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:35
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# IFD.nix\n"
"let\n"
"  drv = derivation {\n"
"    name = \"hello\";\n"
"    builder = \"/bin/sh\";\n"
"    args = [ \"-c\" \"echo -n hello > $out\" ];\n"
"    system = builtins.currentSystem;\n"
"  };\n"
"in \"${builtins.readFile drv} world\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:51
msgid ""
"```\n"
"building '/nix/store/348q1cal6sdgfxs8zqi9v8llrsn4kqkq-hello.drv'...\n"
"\"hello world\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:56
msgid ""
"The contents of the derivation's output have to be [realised](../glossary."
"md#gloss-realise) before they can be read with [`readFile`](./builtins."
"md#builtins-readFile). Only then evaluation can continue to produce the "
"final result."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:59
msgid "Illustration"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:61
msgid ""
"As a first approximation, the following data flow graph shows how evaluation "
"and building are interleaved, if the value of a Nix expression depends on "
"realising a [store object](../store/store-object.md). Boxes are data "
"structures, arrow labels are transformations."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:95
msgid ""
"In more detail, the following sequence diagram shows how the expression is "
"evaluated step by step, and where evaluation is blocked to wait for the "
"build output to appear."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/import-from-derivation.md:97
msgid ""
"```\n"
".-------.     .-------------.                        .---------.\n"
"|Nix CLI|     |Nix evaluator|                        |Nix store|\n"
"'-------'     '-------------'                        '---------'\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |evaluate IFD.nix|                                    |\n"
"    |--------------->|                                    |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |  evaluate `\"${readFile drv} world\"`                 |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |    evaluate `readFile drv`                          |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |   evaluate `drv` as string                          |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |                |instantiate /nix/store/...-hello.drv|\n"
"    |                |----------------------------------->|\n"
"    |                :                                    |\n"
"    |                :  realise /nix/store/...-hello.drv  |\n"
"    |                :----------------------------------->|\n"
"    |                :                                    |\n"
"    |                                                     |--------.\n"
"    |                :                                    |        |\n"
"    |      (evaluation blocked)                           |  echo hello > "
"$out\n"
"    |                :                                    |        |\n"
"    |                                                     |<-------'\n"
"    |                :        /nix/store/...-hello        |\n"
"    |                |<-----------------------------------|\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |  resume `readFile /nix/store/...-hello`             |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |                |   readFile /nix/store/...-hello    |\n"
"    |                |----------------------------------->|\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |                |               hello                |\n"
"    |                |<-----------------------------------|\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |      resume `\"${\"hello\"} world\"`                    |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    |        resume `\"hello world\"`                       |\n"
"    |                |                                    |\n"
"    | \"hello world\"  |                                    |\n"
"    |<---------------|                                    |\n"
".-------.     .-------------.                        .---------.\n"
"|Nix CLI|     |Nix evaluator|                        |Nix store|\n"
"'-------'     '-------------'                        '---------'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
